<title>DENMARK: Danish October consumer confidence +5 (Sept +4).</title>
<headline>Danish October consumer confidence +5 (Sept +4).</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark's consumer confidence indicator was +5 in October, up from +4 in September, the National Statistics Office said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>		   Oct 96	    Sept 96	  Oct 95</p>
<p>			+5		 +4		  +5</p>
<p>NOTE: The survey asks a cross section of Denmark's population its views on current personal and national economic trends, along with consumer intentions for coming months. Changes in consumer confidence are indicated by a higher or lower weighted rating, rather than by index.</p>
<p>--Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969650</p>
